My investigation confirms this only affects the beta clients, as the standard ToolUseBlock response doesn't include the caller field. The issue occurs when taking a tool_use block from a previous API response (which now includes the caller field in v0.75.0) and passing it back into a subsequent request.

PR #1126 and #1135 provide both the type-level correction to remove it from input params and the runtime stripping logic to ensure it doesn't leak into the request payload.

@felixfbecker Thanks for the update! That makes complete sense if the schema has a default value, the generated SDK will always include it in the request payload regardless of whether it was explicitly provided in the input.

Removing the default from the schema is definitely the right long-term fix. For the short term, PR #1135 (which strips it at runtime during transformation) and PR #1126 (which removes it from the input types) serve as a stopgap to unblock users who are seeing this on the current version.

Should I keep those PRs open for now as a safety net, or would you prefer I wait for the schema fix to roll out and propagate to the SDK? I'd be happy to close them if you expect the schema update to land soon.

